# two-at-once.pad — the edges I1 needs: two controls changing in the same frame, and one long hold.
#
# Written for I1's proof of the input layer. Three things this script produces that C5's
# `menu-down-up.pad` cannot:
#
#   * two controls going down in the same pad field, so the capture shows what the game's one-frame
#     event queue does with more than one transition in a frame (the question C5 left open);
#   * two going *up* in the same field, for the release side of the same question;
#   * a hold of over a second, so the ms-held timer runs long enough to show that it accumulates
#     `dt * 1000` in float and chops to an int — the 33, 33, 33, 33, 34 pattern a fixed +33 misses.
#
# Only buttons a menu ignores (the shoulders) and the d-pad, so nothing here can leave the screen it
# started on: no cross, no circle, no triangle, no start. Select is never sent (it is PCSX2's hotkey
# modifier).
#
# Timing is wall-clock, not frame-exact: which frame each edge lands on is not reproducible, and
# nothing that uses this script may depend on it. The capture records the button word per frame, so the
# port is fed what the game actually saw, not what this script asked for.
sleep 500
down l1
down r1
sleep 400
up l1
up r1
sleep 700
down l2
down down
sleep 400
up l2
up down
sleep 700
down r1
sleep 1200
up r1
sleep 500
down up
down l1
down r2
sleep 400
up up
up l1
up r2
sleep 700
press r2 150
sleep 500
